          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em convex powerset of distributions monad
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            (or family of monads) that encompasses both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nondeterministic+computation"} non-determinism
            (via
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability"} probability
            (via
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+distributions"} probability distributions
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The finitary version of the monad is defined as follows. First recall that for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+distributions"} probability distributions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(n)\subseteq [0,1]^n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(n)=\{(r_1,\dots,r_n)\in[0,1]^n | \textstyle \sum_{i=1}^n r_i=1\}
          %p
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+simplex"}
                topological
                = succeed "-simplex" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\subseteq \Delta(n)
            is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+set"} convex
            if it is closed under
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+combinations"} convex combinations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec r\in S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec s\in S
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mover
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a\vec r+(1-a) \vec s)\in S
            for any
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in[0,1]
          %p
            Any finite set of points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mn 1
                  %mi …
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\vec r_1\dots \vec r_k\}\subseteq \Delta(n)
            %em generate
            a convex set (the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+hull"} convex hull
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mn 1
                  %mi …
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi k
                  %mi &amp;
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\vec r_1\dots \vec r_k] = \{
                  a_1\vec r_1 + \dots +a_k\vec r_k |
                  (a_1,\dots, a_k)\in [0,1]^k \&amp; \textstyle \sum_{j=1}^k a_j=1
                  \\}
          %p (Recall that the convex hull is not uniquely determined by such a set of points, since some points in the generating set maybe convex combinations of others.)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(n)
            be the set of finitely generated convex subsets of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(n)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(n)
                has the structure of a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice"} semilattice
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\oplus T
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                closed under convex combinations.
            %li
              %p
                It also has the structure of a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"} convex space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mn 1
                      %mi …
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %msub
                        %mo +
                        %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mn 1
                      %mi …
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\vec r_1\dots \vec r_k]+_p [\vec s_1\dots \vec s_l]
                defined to be
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi p
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi r
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mn 1
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo −
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi s
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                        %mtd
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                        %mtd
                          %mi p
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi r
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mi k
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo −
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi s
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                        %mtd
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                        %mtd
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi p
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi r
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mn 1
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo −
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi s
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mi l
                          %mo ,
                        %mtd
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                        %mtd
                          %mi p
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi r
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mi k
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo −
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi s
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mi l
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{[p\vec r_1+(1-p)\vec s_1,&amp;\dots,&amp;p\vec r_k+(1-p)\vec s_1,\\
                  \\dots,&amp;\dots,&amp;\dots,\\
                  p\vec r_1+(1-p)\vec s_l,&amp;\dots,&amp;p\vec r_k+(1-p)\vec s_l].}
          %p
            We thus build a monad structure for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(n)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi n
                        %mo :
                        %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_n:n\to C(n)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_n(1) = \{(1,0,\dots,0)\}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_n(2) = \{(0,1,\dots,0)\}
            %li
              %p
                The bind, or
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+extension"} Kleisli extension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi m
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:m\to C(n)
                to a function
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:C(m)\to C(n)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mn 1
                  %mi …
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi m
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi …
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi m
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^*([\vec r_1\dots \vec r_k]) =
                  (r_{1,1}f(1)+\dots+r_{1,m}f(m))
                  \\oplus \dots\oplus
                  (r_{k,1}f(1)+\dots+r_{k,m}f(m)).
          %h2#presentation Presentation
          %p
            The finitary convex powerset of distributions monad is presented by an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equational+theory"} equational theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+spaces"} convex spaces
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +_r
            ) together with the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattices"} semilattices
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊕
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus
            ) and the axiom
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mi r
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mi r
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x +_r (y \oplus z) = (x +_r y) \oplus (x +_r z)
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in (0,1)
          %p
            (It may be tempting to think that this is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} distributive law
            of monads, but it is not, because two sets of distributions are equated if they have the same convex hull. For instance,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi y
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo +
                      %mn 0.5
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\oplus y = x \oplus y \oplus (x+_0.5 y)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0.5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0.5
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0.5
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0.5
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0.5
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi y
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0.5
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x \oplus y =
                  (x \oplus y) +_0.5 (x \oplus y)
                  \=
                  (x +_0.5 x)\oplus (x +_0.5 y) \oplus (y +_0.5 x) \oplus (y +_0.5 y)
                  \=
                  x \oplus y \oplus (x +_0.5 y) \ .)
          %p
            The theory is not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebraic+theory"} commutative
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monad"} commutative monad
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0.5
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0.5
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≠
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0.5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (x +_0.5 z) \oplus (y +_0.5 x) \neq
                  (x \oplus y) +_0.5 (z \oplus x)
          %p
            since the right hand side is equal to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
