            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonlinear+probability+theory"} nonlinear probability theory
          %h2#references References
          %p Convex powersets of distributions have been considered by various authors over the last few decades.
          %p A recent extension to metric spaces, including a literature survey is:
          %ul
            %li
              Matteo Mio, Valeria Vignudelli,
              = succeed ",in:" do
                %em Monads and Quantitative Equational Theories for Nondeterminism and Probability
              = succeed "," do
                %em CONCUR 2020
              %strong 171
              (2020) 28:1-28:18, &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.CONCUR.2020.28"}> doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.CONCUR.2020.28
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://hal.science/hal-03028173"} hal:03028173
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.07509"} arXiv:2005.07509
          %p The theory in the finitely generated case is shown to be a “distributive tensor” of probability and non-determinism, and axioms and geometric nature is spelt out in Chapter 6 of:
          %ul
            %li
              Kwok-Ho Cheung,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Distributive Interaction of Algebraic Effects
              = succeed "&rbrack;." do
                %a{:href => "https://ora.ox.ac.uk/objects/uuid:66106628-0a71-4564-bc34-c398db766818"} university archive
          %p The theory is further spelt out, amongst other things, in:
          %ul
            %li
              Filippo Bonchi, Ana Sokolova, Valeria Vignudelli:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Theory of Traces for Systems with Nondeterminism, Probability, and Termination
              %strong 18
              2 (2022) [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.46298/lmcs-18(2:21)2022"}> doi:10.46298/lmcs-18(2:21)2022
              ]
          %p The case with unbounded, infinite joins is earlier considered here:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bart+Jacobs"}> Bart Jacobs
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Coalgebraic trace semantics for combined possibilitistic and probabilistic systems
              %strong 203
              5 (2008) 131-152 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.entcs.2008.05.023"}> doi:10.1016/j.entcs.2008.05.023
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+theory"} domain theory
          %ul
            %li
              Daniela Varacca:
              = succeed "." do
                %em Probability, Nondeterminism and Concurrency: Two Denotational Models for Probabilistic Computation
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRICS"} BRICS
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.brics.dk/DS/03/14"} brics:DS/03/14
          %p and analyzed as “convex powercones” by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+W.+Mislove"}> Michael W. Mislove
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nondeterminism and probabilistic choice: Obeying the laws
              %p
                2000, Lecture Notes in Computer Science
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1877
                = succeed "&rbrack;." do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-44618-4_26"} doi:10.1007/3-540-44618-4_26
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Regina+Tix"}> Regina Tix
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Keimel"} Klaus Keimel
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+D.+Plotkin"} Gordon D. Plotkin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Semantic domains for combining probability and non-determinism
                %strong 222
                (2009) 3–99 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.entcs.2009.01.002"}> doi:10.1016/j.entcs.2009.01.002
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
